"is_error": false, "num_turns": 4, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The spec is implemented and the check it lists passes: `pytest -q tests/test_logs_store.py tests/test_openai_responses.py tests/test_migrate.py tests/test_llm_logs.py` gives 266 passed. The implementer also ran the full suite (998 passed); I only ran the listed command myself.\n\nI read through the whole diff and it matches the spec. No changes were needed from me.\n\n- **`pyproject.toml`**: the dependency is now `condense-json>=1.1`.\n- **`llm/migrations.py`**: a new migration, `m027_turns_response_json`, adds a nullable `turns.response_json` column.\n- **`llm/logs.py`**:\n  - `LogStore.log` now saves the provider's raw payload in that column, condensed: long strings and blocks the turn's messages, tools or schema already hold are stored as short references.\n  - The new `LogStore.turn_response_json` rebuilds the full payload. It raises an error if a reference no longer resolves.\n  - `llm logs --json` now shows `response_json` instead of always `null`. If one turn's payload can't be rebuilt, that row shows `null` and the rest of the listing still works.\n- **`llm/default_plugins/openai_models.py`**: when streaming, both the sync and async Responses models now update the reasoning part with the encrypted reasoning from the final response. The stored part and `response_json` now agree, and there is still only one reasoning part.\n\nThe test files were not edited. The implementer noted that `ruff format --check` already failed on three of the touched files before this change, so formatting was left as it was.", "ttft_ms": 2576, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 457816, "uuid": "cc735a5f-30d3-41ad-9e36-6c8bfff39604", "ttft_stream_ms": 2065, "time_to_request_ms": 385, "first_content_frame_ms": 2066, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
